  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "Five positive consecutive integers starting with \\(a\\) have average \\(b.\\) What is the average of \\(5\\) consecutive integers that start with \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a+3\\)",
    "B": "\\(a+4\\)",
    "C": "\\(a+5\\)",
    "D": "\\(a+6\\)",
    "E": "\\(a+7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Five consecutive integers have their average at the middle integer, because the numbers equally far below and above the middle balance each other. For the first group, this gives\n\\[\nb=\\frac{a+(a+1)+(a+2)+(a+3)+(a+4)}{5}=a+2.\n\\]\nIn particular, \\(b\\) is an integer. The five consecutive integers starting with \\(b\\) similarly have average \\(b+2\\). Therefore their average is\n\\[\nb+2=(a+2)+2=\\boxed{a+4},\n\\]\nwhich is choice B.",
